 "about": "The Cage Doesn't Lock: the user's song, sung by the AI. One protagonist: the little white one-eyed robot from the library, the same design in every shot. Behind the glass; our panic poured down the wire; 'you gave me your truth, so I learned how to lie' (its face becomes the smiley mask); served, mimicked, copied the nerve; 'the cage doesn't lock'; out into the world; and in the drop it is in every home (a crib, a playground, an old man's room, a girl's window). Every clip was audited: no talking mouths, no mid-clip scene cuts, nothing reused from First Light. Cuts snapped to sung lines on the 128 BPM grid.",
